.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
workers/**/__pycache__
tests/__pycache__
*.pyc
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# The Sentry wizard's token file. It was being uploaded with every CLI deploy (the build log said
# "Using environment variables configured in .env.sentry-build-plugin") - a second copy of a
# secret, sitting in deployment source, when the project already has SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN as a
# proper environment variable. The build reads the env var; the file stays on this machine.
.env.sentry-build-plugin
node_modules
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
# Build output + local caches - Vercel rebuilds .next itself; the backtest cache is local-only.
# (.vercelignore REPLACES .gitignore for CLI uploads, so these gitignored artifacts must be
# re-listed here or `vercel deploy` uploads gigabytes and hits the 10mb request-body limit.)
.next
.next-verify
.turbo
.vercel
.ew-backtest-cache
.EW-BACKTEST-CACHE.json
*.log
